    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d162">

                <pb facs="0281" n="211" sameAs="frus:frus1862/pg211"/>

                <head>Mr. Seward to Mr. Adams.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 369.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State,</hi>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington,</hi></placeName>
                        <date calendar="gregorian" when="1862-10-03"><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >October</hi> 13, 1862.</date></dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir:</hi> Your despatch of the 25th of September (No.
                    225) has been received and submitted to the President. While its statements are
                    very interesting, and its suggestions seem to be wise and judicious, a special
                    reply on my part has been rendered unnecessary by my anticipation of the subject
                    discussed in your despatches.</p>
                <p>I am, sir, your obedient servant,</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>WILLIAM H. SEWARD.</signed></closer>
                <postscript>
                    <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Charles Francis Adams,</hi> Esq., <hi
                            rendition="#italic">&amp;c., &amp;c., &amp;c.</hi></p>
                </postscript>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
